findings.problem:
Only shared behavior is declared unchanged; there is no inventory of the Codex-visible changes:
- own-declared arbitrary caller keys with any value, currently passed by native_environment, become rejected;
- foreign-declared baseline credentials switch from silent stripping to refusal;
- provider env_key/header restoration is removed;
- own invalid refs (currently InvalidInput) and undeclared caller keys (currently OwnershipMismatch) move to the opaque InvalidConfiguration category;
- baseline capture moves from launch to construction.
Existing LaunchRequest.environment producers (Workflow forwarding, direct component callers and fixtures) are not enumerated.

findings.required_fix:
Add an impact-analysis section that lists:
- each changed Codex behavior, with old and new outcome and error kind;
- every current producer and consumer of the caller map or ambient baseline;
- the intended test migrations;
- the areas expected to be unaffected, each with its basis.
